# Supply Chain

This project follows a defense-in-depth supply-chain posture. Every rule
here is enforced — not aspirational.

## Container base images

Mainstream public images, digest-pinned. The full digest (`@sha256:...`)
is required in every Dockerfile, `docker-compose.yml`, and any image
list inside `scripts/audit-all.sh`. The tag alone (e.g. `python:3.14-slim`)
is never enough.

Approved bases (pin the digest, then track via Renovate):

- Python: `python:3.14-slim@sha256:...`
- Node: `node:24-alpine@sha256:...`
- nginx (static serve): `nginx:alpine@sha256:...`
- Caddy (reverse proxy): `caddy:2-alpine@sha256:...`
- Postgres (compose only): `postgres:16-alpine@sha256:...`
- uv binary stage (when needed): `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:<ver>@sha256:...`

Forbidden: bare tags (`python:3.14-slim` with no digest), `latest`,
`cgr.dev/chainguard/*` (deprecated in this harness), `bitnami/*`,
random community images.

Use multi-stage builds. Run as a non-root user in the runtime stage
(`USER 1000:1000` or a named user). Builder stage may use root for
`apk add` / `apt-get`; runtime stage must not.

## Dependency lockfiles

- Python: `uv.lock` is committed and authoritative. Allowed installs:
  - `uv sync --frozen` (CI, Docker, fresh clone)
  - `scripts/safe-uv.sh add <pkg>` (audited; rejects new advisories)
  - `scripts/safe-uv.sh lock --upgrade` (audited)
- JS: `pnpm-lock.yaml` is committed and authoritative. Allowed installs:
  - `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (CI, Docker, fresh clone)
  - `scripts/safe-pnpm.sh add <pkg>` (audited; rejects new advisories)

`pip install`, `npm install`, `yarn install`, and bare `uv add` /
`pnpm add` outside the safe-wrappers are forbidden — including
throwaway scripts and Dockerfiles.

The safe-wrappers snapshot the lockfile, run the operation, re-audit,
and restore the lockfile if any new advisory of any severity is
introduced.

## Network install patterns

`curl <url> | sh` is forbidden in Dockerfiles, scripts, and CI. If a
tool requires it, propose an alternative (Wolfi/Alpine package, distro
package, or a pinned download with SHA verification).

GitHub Actions are pinned. `actions/checkout@v5` is acceptable (major
version with security commitments). `@main` or `@master` is not. Third-
party actions must be pinned to a commit SHA.

## Pre-commit checks (blocking)

Configured in `lefthook.yml` and `scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit`:

- `gitleaks git --staged -c .gitleaks.toml` — secrets on the staged diff
- `semgrep` with `p/typescript` + `p/python` — SAST on staged source files
- Conditional `scripts/audit-all.sh` when staged files touch lockfiles,
  Dockerfiles, or the audit tooling itself

A commit cannot be made if any of the above fail. Do not advise the user
to bypass with `--no-verify`. If a check is failing wrongly, fix the
check, the allowlist (`.gitleaks.toml`, `.semgrepignore`, `.trivyignore`),
or the file — don't bypass.

Emergency bypass envs (documented; not for routine use):
- `SKIP_STATIC_SCAN=1` — skips gitleaks + semgrep
- `SKIP_GITLEAKS=1`, `SKIP_SEMGREP=1` — granular
- `SKIP_AUDIT=1` — skips supply-chain audit only

## scripts/audit-all.sh

The orchestrator. Modes:

- `scripts/audit-all.sh` — lockfile audits (osv-scanner, pip-audit,
  pnpm audit) + full-tree gitleaks + semgrep
- `--with-images` — additionally scan digest-pinned bases with Trivy
  (HIGH/CRITICAL, OS packages, ignore-unfixed; gated by `.trivyignore`)
- `--with-images-informational` — same scans, image findings do not
  change the exit code (used in scheduled CI)
- `--supply-chain-only` — lockfiles + Trivy only (used from the
  pre-commit hook after staged gitleaks/semgrep already ran)

Required tools: `osv-scanner`, `pip-audit`, `pnpm` (web template only),
`uv`, `trivy`, `gitleaks`, `semgrep`. The wrappers never auto-install
tools — they print `brew install …` hints and exit 127 if missing.

## CI checks

- Backend job: `uv sync --frozen` → ruff → pyright → pytest → pip-audit
- Frontend job (web): pnpm install → eslint → vue-tsc → vitest →
  `pnpm audit`
- Static-scan job: gitleaks + semgrep on the full tree (catches PRs
  that bypassed local hooks)
- Audit job (scheduled, daily): `scripts/audit-all.sh
  --with-images-informational` against the pinned digests

cosign / Sigstore verification is **not** used. The trust model is:
digest-pinned mainstream image + Trivy + Renovate, not signature
attestation.

## Renovate

`renovate.json` configures Renovate to:

- Auto-merge dev-tooling minor/patch updates after CI passes
- Open PRs for app-dep major versions (override the no-PR rule for
  bot-driven updates)
- Pin GitHub Actions to SHAs (`pinDigests: true`)
- Pin Docker image digests (`pinDigests: true` for the docker manager)

## Forbidden practices

- Editing `uv.lock` or `pnpm-lock.yaml` by hand
- Committing `.env` or any file matching `*.pem`, `*.key`, `id_rsa*`
- Hardcoding API keys or tokens in source, even as "TODO replace later"
- `chmod -R` in Dockerfiles
- `ADD <url>` in Dockerfiles (use multi-stage with explicit verification)
- Bypassing the safe-wrappers (`uv add` / `pnpm add` directly)
- Bare image tags in Dockerfiles or compose (always `@sha256:...`)
